From 0c86800c2b6cc7effaf42eb8e4cb44da43f20338 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oldrich Klimanek <oldrich.klimanek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:17:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] integrals: evaluate Bose-Einstein and Fermi-Dirac definite
 integrals

Add sympy/integrals/bosefermi.py, which evaluates the definite integrals

    Integral(x**p/(exp(a*x + b) - 1), (x, 0, oo))   (bosons)
    Integral(x**p/(exp(a*x + b) + 1), (x, 0, oo))   (fermions)

in closed form using gamma, zeta (or dirichlet_eta) and polylog.  For b = 0
the results reduce to Gamma(p+1)*zeta(p+1) and Gamma(p+1)*eta(p+1); the
special value p = 0, b = 0 for fermions is log(2).

The Meijer G machinery cannot handle these integrands: the Mellin transform
of 1/(exp(a*x + b) - 1) is a**(-s)*gamma(s)*zeta(s), which is not a Meijer G
function.  Hook the new evaluator into _meijerint_definite_2, before the
G-function rewriting is attempted; meijerint_definite already returns results
that do not contain meijerg.

The matcher also normalises scaled denominators A*exp(a*x + b) + C (which
covers e.g. exp(2*x + 0.3), automatically expanded by SymPy into
1.3498...*exp(2*x) + 1) and rejects forms where the integral diverges
(a <= 0, p <= -1, or b < 0 for bosons).
